MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DG-004a. Add the register-computation instruction set (no memory, no faults)
and restore/repair the differential readout so the three-way differential
(interp/QEMU/gem5) coverage grows from 6 to 77 cases with DIVERGE=0.

Fixes to the incoming batch:
  * Regression: restored the DG-003a halt-time DADAO_REGDUMP hook (had been
    dropped in the rewrite -> adapter saw no final state -> add/addi coverage
    fell to 0). This was the "add/addi decode regression".
  * jump: PC = (instAddr+4) + (imm<<2)  (rb0=PC+4, spec §5.3/§1.3) — was missing +4.
  * add/sub: true 128-bit rdha:rdhb = sext128(rdhc) ± sext128(rdhd)  (spec §3.5) —
    was a 1-bit carry approximation (wrong hi for negatives).
  * cseq/csne: false branch leaves rdhc unchanged (old value), condition is
    EQ/NE(rdha,rdhb), dest is rdhc  (spec §3.12) — was writing rdha on false.
  * exts/extz: (x<<amt)>>amt with amt=hd[5:0], amt=0 => identity  (spec §3.11) —
    removed a s?s:64 branch that shifted by 64 (UB) and broke amt=0.
  * csn/csz/csp and cseq/csne: operand-index tracking so a cond/true/false
    operand that is rd0 reads as 0 (spec §1.2 rd0==0) instead of a shifted operand.

Implemented (spec-derived, no QEMU translate.c): logic (and/orr/xor/xnor §3.10),
shift/extend reg+imm (shlu/shrs/shru/exts/extz §3.11), compare reg+imm
(cmps/cmpu §3.8/§3.9), conditional assign (csn/csz/csp/cseq/csne §3.12), muls/mulu
(§3.7), sub (§3.5), wyde immediate (setzw/setow/orw/andnw §3.13), RB add/sub/addi
(§4.3/§4.4) and rela (§4.8). MISC-Norm (op 0x10) sub-decoded by ha per §2.8.1.

gen_min_elf loads at 0x80000000 to match the QEMU harness base and interpreter
DEFAULT_PC, so PC-relative results (rela, jump) agree across the differential.

3 smokes unchanged (42/42/0); block-copy (rd2rd/rd2rb/...), memory and
fault-expecting vectors remain SKIP for DG-004b/c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
